de_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODI3Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58827791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier","html_url":"https://github.com/Bryan-Meier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bryan-Meier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T00:40:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T00:40:37Z","body":"What makes this even more annoying is that it is in fact possible but just not with GitHub Copilot.\n\nI have a 2600 line JSON file that I wanted to sort the array of objects based on the value of an element. This fails in GitHub Copilot with the length limit error. I can go to ChatGPT, upload the same file and ask the same question and I get the a fully sorted file. So, I would argue against the idea @hmorneau mentioned where that LLM's are optimized for 200 to 250 lines maximum. The fact is LLM's can and do handle large quantities of output. It's just the GitHub Copilot does not.\n\nBecause of issues like this, I find myself using ChatGPT 90% of the time and Copilot the other 10%.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2699360440/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2703120775","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/3927#issuecomment-2703120775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/3927","id":2703120775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6hHlmH","user":{"login":"Eyalm321","id":145741922,"node_id":"U_kgDOCK_YYg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145741922?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321","html_url":"https://github.com/Eyalm321","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eyalm321/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T08:15:52Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T08:15:52Z","body":"Guys how do you want to beat cursor if there is a length limit on normal size projects, games for youtube is fun and all but we need to get some work done.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2703120775/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2703159780","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/3927#issuecomment-2703159780","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/3927","id":2703159780,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6hHvHk","user":{"login":"JS3910","id":31373791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMzczNzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31373791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910","html_url":"https://github.com/JS3910","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JS3910/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T08:34:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T08:34:58Z","body":"Just to be perfectly clear and specific: I am aware that LLM's have limitations on prompt context size and that there are ways to work around this sometimes. \n\nMy point is that an error message that says the RESPONSE to a question was too long is a nonsensical error. We don't generate the response. We don't know how long it would've been. We don't know how long it's allowed to be. We don't know what prompt was sent to the LLM. We don't know what parts of that prompt would cause output to be too long. \n\nTelling the user that something didn't work and the only way to fix it is to unspecifically alter your input in such a way that the copilot black box hopefully generates a shorter answer is an absurd, borderline surrealistic instruction.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/v